    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #277\n\n- 2026-09-16 09:15Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-16 09:34Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #411 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-277-review-debt-12-12-bound-the-code-revie-thr_wsmm5kk6td`. ## Summary This closes out the last of the review-debt batch (12/12), addressing the three outstanding findings from PR #42 and #43 that were never fixed on `develop`: - **`.github/workflows/code-review.yml`**: the `curl` that installs the Claude Code CLI now has `--connect-timeout 10 --max-time 60`, so an unresponsive install endpoint fails the step quickly instead of hanging until the job's `timeout-minutes: 60` fires. - **`.github/workflows/release.yml`**: `permissions: contents: write` moved from workflow level to the `release` job, so any job added later starts with no inherited write access. - **`.github/workflows/release.yml`**: the version guard now also rejects the literal `\"null\"` that `jq -r` prints when `backend/package.json` has no `.version` field, failing the step with a clear error instead of tagging a `vnull` release. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was not touched, per scope. Verification: both YAML files were validated with `yaml-lint`, and since these workflow files have no dedicated test harness, verification is by inspection as the issue specifies. I also ran the full project pipelines to confirm no regressions: `backend/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 277 unit + 1180 integration + 5 e2e tests) and `web/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 187 tests) both passed with exit code 0. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-16 09:58Z — Relay BB run is blocked and needs manual follow-up — it will not be retried automatically. Reason: could not request a re-run for code-review check \"code-review\": GitHub API /actions/runs/35080195408/rerun failed (403): {\"message\":\"Resource not accessible by integration\",\"documentation_url\":\"https://docs.github.com/rest/actions/workflow-runs#re-run-a-workflow\",\"status\":\"403\"} — manual follow-up needed: https://github.com/dvdtrsnk/semprec/runs/104742194955 Pushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-277-review-debt-12-12-bound-the-code-revie-thr_wsmm5kk6td`. ## Summary This closes out the last of the review-debt batch (12/12), addressing the three outstanding findings from PR #42 and #43 that were never fixed on `develop`: - **`.github/workflows/code-review.yml`**: the `curl` that installs the Claude Code CLI now has `--connect-timeout 10 --max-time 60`, so an unresponsive install endpoint fails the step quickly instead of hanging until the job's `timeout-minutes: 60` fires. - **`.github/workflows/release.yml`**: `permissions: contents: write` moved from workflow level to the `release` job, so any job added later starts with no inherited write access. - **`.github/workflows/release.yml`**: the version guard now also rejects the literal `\"null\"` that `jq -r` prints when `backend/package.json` has no `.version` field, failing the step with a clear error instead of tagging a `vnull` release. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was not touched, per scope. Verification: both YAML files were validated with `yaml-lint`, and since these workflow files have no dedicated test harness, verification is by inspection as the issue specifies. I also ran the full project pipelines to confirm no regressions: `backend/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 277 unit + 1180 integration + 5 e2e tests) and `web/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 187 tests) both passed with exit code 0. Relay-Step-Status: pass Remove the `agent:blocked` label from this issue once it's addressed to let Relay pick it up again.",
